    {"id": "zh_logistics4x4_page", "label": "Logistics 4x4 page (Chinese)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/zh/logistics4x4.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null},
    {"id": "zh_presenter_page", "label": "Kameleon Presenter page (Chinese)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/zh/presenter.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null},
    {"id": "vi_index_chameleon_ai_platform", "label": "Chameleon AI Platform", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One PyQt6 desktop app bundling eight disciplines (IDE, presenter, accounting, trading, classroom, P2P networking) running locally without cloud dependence; local-first privacy is the stated design driver."},
    {"id": "vi_presenter_kameleon_presenter", "label": "Kameleon Presenter (theatre metaphor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/presenter.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Slides are the Stage, content blocks are Actors, transitions are Cues; 0-10,000 logical coordinates make presentations resolution-independent; .kpt ZIP bundles make projects portable."},
    {"id": "vi_companion_companion_app", "label": "Chameleon Companion App (Android bridge)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/companion.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single persistent WebSocket bridge (port 8770 via chameleon_mobile_bridge.py) carries eight independent channels - AI chat, P2P video, presenter remote, screen mirror, files, media, receipts, voice - as typed JSON messages."},
    {"id": "vi_companion_sim_call_bridge", "label": "SIM Call Bridge (hardware call merge)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/companion.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registers the WebRTC call with Android's telecom stack alongside a SIM call so the native Merge Calls option does audio mixing in phone hardware - earpiece-only and private; Bluetooth SCO routing is the fallback when the carrier lacks hardware conferencing."},
    {"id": "vi_companion_tailscale_mesh", "label": "Tailscale mesh networking", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/companion.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All channels run on a private Tailscale network: no ports open to the public internet, WireGuard end-to-end encryption, and no cloud relay fees; lan_video.py UDP/WebSocket transport is the LAN fallback."},
    {"id": "vi_logistics4x4_logistics_4x4", "label": "Logistics 4x4 (cross-border fleet comms)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/logistics4x4.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not a replacement for enterprise logistics platforms - it fills the gap for small operators and sole traders: 4 SIM callers plus 4 P2P video peers in one call space, on standard Android phones, working at remote border crossings where enterprise apps assume fast reliable data."},
    {"id": "vi_codes_field_comms_protocol", "label": "Field Comms Code Protocol (letter + two digits)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/codes.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compact codes (category letter + two-digit severity, 99 always most severe) usable over SMS when no data connectivity exists; three profiles (D Driver, H Hiker, X Emergency Services) share universal A alert and Z system vocabularies so cross-agency interop survives degraded conditions; A99+H99 is the universal SOS."},
    {"id": "vi_codes_methane_framework", "label": "METHANE major-incident framework / P1-P4 triage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/codes.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The X-profile aligns with the international P1-P4 triage scale and METHANE major-incident declaration framework so paramedics and SAR coordinators recognise the terminology immediately."},
    {"id": "vi_accounting_uk_accounting", "label": "UK double-entry accounting module", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/accounting.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Local SQLite ledger targeting HMRC Making Tax Digital; VAT codes S20/R5/Z/E/O; UK tax year 6 Apr - 5 Apr; HMRC Notice 700 compliant invoicing; all reports emit structured JSON so the AI can parse and advise."},
    {"id": "vi_classroom_language_classroom", "label": "Language Classroom (WebRTC teaching)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/classroom.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Full-mesh WebRTC group video for 4+ students with no central media server; integrated payments (Stripe GBP primary, Alipay for Chinese students, PayPal fallback); UK call-recording law (RIPA 2000) requires notifying all parties, so a RECORDING banner is shown."},
    {"id": "vi_classroom_chameleon_signal_server", "label": "Chameleon signal server (chameleon_signal.py)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/classroom.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Handles WebRTC SDP/ICE relay on port 8766 and also runs inside Termux on Android, so a phone can be both client and signalling node - no cloud relay required."},
    {"id": "uk_services_ai_web_services", "label": "AI Web Services (build, domain, hosting, manage, growth)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/uk/services.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five tiers: AI website builder from project files, DNS/domain configuration, free hosting (GitHub Pages, Cloudflare, Netlify/Vercel, Tailscale Funnel self-host), AI-managed inbox, and SEO/growth. Domain configuration is Service 2 because DNS proved the most confusing step in the developer's own testing."},
    {"id": "uk_technician_ai_pc_technician", "label": "AI PC Technician (diagnostics + USB driver porter)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/uk/technician.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Surgical repair protocol: diagnose before touching, non-destructive first, verify each step, dead-man's switch with @reboot resume for reboot-requiring actions. USB driver porter picks Path A (udev/modprobe), B (userspace hidraw/ALSA), or C (full kernel module with DKMS + ARM cross-compile) based on how proprietary the device protocol is."},
    {"id": "vi_ide_ai_command_bridge", "label": "AI Command Bridge (structured JSON editor control)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "/mnt/sda2/website/vi/ide.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The AI operates the editor via structured JSON: read a file once, then anchor-based replace_text edits (anchors survive line-number drift); .bak backup before write_file overwrites; all returned file/terminal/web content is wrapped in [UNTRUSTED_CONTENT] markers to block prompt injection."}
  ],
